From: Local system integration <local@nixos>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86/amd/pmc: quirk HP 14-fq1xxx NVMe resume SMI

The HP Laptop 14-fq1xxx (board 887C) has the same firmware-assisted
NVMe D3-to-D0 path as the AMD laptops already covered by
amd_pmc_skip_nvme_smi_handler().  Its DSDT defines SI3R in PM80 at
0xfed80380 and the NVMe power resource checks that bit before issuing
APMC commands 0xd1 and 0xd8.

On BIOS F.38 this SMI stops all concurrent noirq resume work for about
10.2 seconds.  The delay is visible simultaneously in the NVMe, xHCI,
and HDA PCI callbacks, so changing any one of those drivers would only
mask the platform defect.

Select the existing combined quirk for this model.  Clearing SI3R in
the AMD PMC restore-early hook avoids the firmware SMI before NVMe is
returned to D0, while retaining the Cezanne spurious-8042 workaround.

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/amd/pmc/pmc-quirks.c b/drivers/platform/x86/amd/pmc/pmc-quirks.c
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/amd/pmc/pmc-quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/amd/pmc/pmc-quirks.c
@@ -223,6 +223,15 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id fwbug_list[] = {
 		}
 	},
+	{
+		.ident = "HP Laptop 14-fq1xxx",
+		.driver_data = &quirk_s2idle_spurious_8042,
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "HP"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "HP Laptop 14-fq1xxx"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "887C"),
+		}
+	},
 	/* https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/issues/2684 */
 	{
 		.ident = "HP Laptop 15s-eq2xxx",
 		.driver_data = &quirk_s2idle_spurious_8042,
